CRASH-13: do not close the project's output file in writeresults

writeresults() reads results through out->OutFile when the output file
is still open (EN_report called before EN_closeQ), or opens the file by
name otherwise, and then fcloses whichever handle it used. In the first
case out->OutFile is left pointing at a closed stream: a second
EN_report reads nothing (all-zero tables) or another file that reuses
the FILE structure, and EN_closeQ closes the stream again. Close the
file only if writeresults() opened it.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply CRASH-13_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/report.c b/src/report.c
index 2ea72a8..29d95ce 100644
--- a/src/report.c
+++ b/src/report.c
@@ -639,8 +639,9 @@ int writeresults(Project *pr)
         }
     }
 
-    // Free output file
-    if (outFile != NULL)
+    // Close output file if it was opened here
+    // (the project's own OutFile is closed by closeoutfile)
+    if (outFile != NULL && outFile != out->OutFile)
     {
         fclose(outFile);
         outFile = NULL;
